{"id":417,"date":"2020-10-22T13:20:59","date_gmt":"2020-10-22T20:20:59","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=417"},"modified":"2024-08-30T10:08:20","modified_gmt":"2024-08-30T17:08:20","slug":"cdmb-pairing","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/cdmb-pairing\/","title":{"rendered":"0D: Pair to Blockly"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213d1f05ca\" name=\"6a2213d1f05ca\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Pairing your drone in Blockly<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]When you use the remote control, the drone and remote pair automatically once you turn them on. To use Blockly with CoDrone Mini, you will have to do a few new steps to set up your computer. Don&#8217;t worry! We will walk you through all the steps so you can get to coding!<\/p>\n<p>If you prefer a video walkthrough, click <a href=\"https:\/\/drive.google.com\/file\/d\/1R-rLwWl0vMEj4PSTcaSUHf2ZK3dmYaD6\/view\">here<\/a>.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213d1f06f3\" name=\"6a2213d1f06f3\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Device Requirements<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<strong>Windows<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>You should be running <strong>Windows 10 or later<\/strong>. To check, hold down the Windows + R keys and search for &#8220;winver&#8221;. The version you are running of Windows 10 will appear on the window. You may need to update Windows if you have a version below 1703.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;448&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;449&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>MacOS<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>If you are using Mac OS, you should have 2012 hardware or newer and your machine should be enabled with Bluetooth. To check this, go to About this Mac &gt; System Report&#8230; &gt; Bluetooth.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;451&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;452&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;453&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>Chromebooks\/Chrome browser<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Your Google Chrome should be version 89 or later<\/strong>, but ideally updated to the most recent version. If you are not sure how to check, click on the Chrome menu on the top right, scroll down to &#8220;Help&#8221;, and select &#8220;About Google Chrome&#8221;. Google Chrome might automatically update. If not, please update Chrome.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;457&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;4356&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]For more about Blockly minimum requirements, please visit\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.robolink.com\/blockly-min-requirements\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-link-type=\"LINK\">https:\/\/www.robolink.com\/blockly-min-requirements\/<\/a>.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213d1f0749\" name=\"6a2213d1f0749\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Connect the remote and power the drone<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Once you are sure you&#8217;ve met the requirements, plug the CoDrone Mini remote into this computer\u2019s USB port <span class=\"bold\">with the provided USB cable<\/span> (some cables can transfer power, but not data). Also, power on the CoDrone Mini, and make sure the CoDrone Mini and remote are paired. This is indicated by the CoDrone Mini\u2019s LED and the remote LED being solid (not blinking).[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;2333&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213d1f079f\" name=\"6a2213d1f079f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Finding your device<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<strong>Note:<\/strong> If at any point during this step you encounter some difficulty, see Step 5. You may be missing a driver or Google Chrome may be outdated.<\/p>\n<p>Try restarting Chrome and go back to the Blockly page. Click on \u201cPair\u201d in the pairing menu, and a list of devices should pop up. Look for a USB port &#8212;\u00a0 on Macs this will be something like USB-Serial, and on Windows this will look like COM.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;434&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]This may take some trial and error on your part, but the good news is that if you pick the wrong port, you will get a notification that Blockly was unable to pair![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;430&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]If you pick the correct port, you will see \u201cPaired: CoDrone Mini\u201d in the pairing menu.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;429&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213d1f089f\" name=\"6a2213d1f089f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Troubleshooting<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>If you saw Bluetooth devices but not USB ports come up in your pairing list, first make sure you are using the USB cable that came with the kit or any USB that is\u00a0<strong>not charge-only<\/strong>. You may also need to try various USB ports.<\/p>\n<p>If you are still having issues finding and pairing to the device, you might need to install the driver. This will help your computer find the CoDrone Mini remote. You can use either of these links for driver installation:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/drive.google.com\/file\/d\/1ge1JZaClAL1ERtx7ATJFxvAFaHGX8VBM\/view?usp=sharing\">Windows driver<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/drive.google.com\/file\/d\/1a2NPQoyjvr8hwWxO1I5T-ZFowznYsx9E\/view\">macOS driver<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/github.com\/juliagoda\/CH341SER\">Linux driver<\/a><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>If you are a student using a school computer, you may need to have your teacher grant you access to install the driver.<\/p>\n<p>If you are on a Mac, you may need to give permission for the driver to access the remote. Go to System Preferences &gt; Security &amp; Privacy, and then click &#8220;Allow&#8221;. The name will be &#8220;Jiangsu Qinheng Co., Ltd.&#8221;.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"activity2__spacer\">\n<div class=\"activity2__step-media\">If you are using a Linux device, please use <a href=\"https:\/\/learn.sparkfun.com\/tutorials\/how-to-install-ch340-drivers\/linux\">this guide<\/a> on how to install the driver on your device.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;436&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;437&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213d1f0939\" name=\"6a2213d1f0939\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>All set!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Your device is now ready to use Blockly with CoDrone Mini! Next time you want to pair with CoDrone Mini, you don&#8217;t have to set up the experimental flags anymore. Just plug and play!<br \/>\nYou will only need to do these steps again if you switch to a new computer. See the next lesson to learn more about Blockly.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 7 Pairing your drone in Blockly [vc_column_text]When you use the remote control, the drone and remote pair automatically once you turn them on. To use Blockly with CoDrone&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/cdmb-pairing\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1688,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":407,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[2164,2125,2107],"class_list":["post-417","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-codrone-mini","lesson-tag-pairing","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/417","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":26,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/417\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":10872,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/417\/revisions\/10872"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1688"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\